Patch 10 (DRAFT, 2026-10-28, not applied, SDK not built): rex_xr_sample_hands + rex_xr_hands_aim.

Adds both motion controllers to DK_XR (patch 09's xr_output.cpp), for the game's hand IK:
- one action set "dk_hands": grip_pose + aim_pose, subaction paths /user/hand/left and /user/hand/right,
  suggested for khr/simple, oculus/touch, valve/index, htc/vive, microsoft/motion (each one the runtime
  refuses is skipped), attached once right after the reference spaces in Start(); one action space per
  hand per pose. Any failure logs "[XR] hands OFF: ..." and leaves the headset path untouched.
- rex_xr_sample_hands(id, grip_left[7], grip_right[7], flags): xrSyncActions once per call (only while the
  session is FOCUSED, tracked in PollEvents), then xrGetActionStatePose + xrLocateSpace of each grip space
  in the SAME local space and at the SAME predicted time as rex_xr_sample_head. Pose = px py pz qx qy qz qw.
  flags = DK_XR_HAND_* bits (header). rex_xr_hands_aim(id, ...) returns the aim poses of that call.
- exported exactly like rex_xr_sample_head (extern "C" __declspec(dllexport) in rexgpu-xenos.dll); the game
  looks them up with GetProcAddress(GetModuleHandleW(L"rexgpu-xenos.dll"), "rex_xr_sample_hands").

Against: rexglue-sdk working tree on the home PC with patch 09/09b applied (xr_output.h/.cpp as of
2026-10-28). Checked: `git apply --check` on copies of those two files passes; both the old and the new
xr_output.cpp pass `clang++ -std=c++20 -fsyntax-only -Wall` (llvm-mingw, SDL3's bundled OpenXR headers).
Not built with the SDK's own toolchain, not run.

